{"crc":"b0d7f8a2","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the LaTeX printer for `Poly` doesn't use the same order of monomials as `str` and `pretty` printers. The `str` and `pretty` printers use `expr.terms()` which returns terms in the logical order (from highest to lowest degrees), but the LaTeX printer needs to be fixed to do the same.\n\nLet me find the `_print_Poly` method in the LaTeX printer file:\n\n```python\n# path: sympy/printing/latex.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    def _print_Poly(self, poly):\n        cls = poly.__class__.__name__\n        expr = poly.as_expr()\n        gens = list(map(self._print, poly.gens))\n        domain = poly.domain\n\n        args = \", \".join([self._print(expr)] + gens)\n        if domain != ZZ:\n            args = args + \", domain=%s\" % self._print(domain)\n\n        return r\"\\operatorname{%s}{\\left( %s \\right)}\" % (cls, args)\n=======\n    def _print_Poly(self, poly):\n        cls = poly.__class__.__name__\n        terms = []\n        for monom, coeff in poly.terms():\n            s_monom = []\n            for i, exp in enumerate(monom):\n                if exp > 0:\n                    if exp == 1:\n                        s_monom.append(poly.gens[i])\n                    else:\n                        s_monom.append(poly.gens[i]**exp)\n            s_monom = Mul(*s_monom)\n            if coeff.is_Add:\n                if s_monom:\n                    s_coeff = \"(\" + self._print(coeff) + \")\"\n                else:\n                    s_coeff = self._print(coeff)\n            else:\n                if s_monom:\n                    if coeff is S.One:\n                        terms.append(s_monom)\n                        continue\n                    if coeff is S.NegativeOne:\n                        terms.append(-s_monom)\n                        continue\n                s_coeff = self._print(coeff)\n            if not s_monom:\n                s_term = s_coeff\n            else:\n                s_term = s_coeff + \" \" + self._print(s_monom)\n            terms.append(s_term)\n        expr = Add(*terms)\n        gens = list(map(self._print, poly.gens))\n        domain = poly.domain\n\n        args = \", \".join([self._print(expr)] + gens)\n        if domain != ZZ:\n            args = args + \", domain=%s\" % self._print(domain)\n\n        return r\"\\operatorname{%s}{\\left( %s \\right)}\" % (cls, args)\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZT290RM4KEVBQQR6KGHJ87B","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZT290RFN4YZ72A94AN5YGP2"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786507482.474244}
